# Agent-harness state is local and machine-generated: tool-installed skill
# copies (`tkt init`) and per-session workflow scripts. The repository's own
# agent contract is the tracked `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` at the root, not
# anything under these directories. Nothing here has ever been tracked; add
# shared harness configuration deliberately with `git add -f` rather than by
# narrowing this rule, so a generated artifact cannot arrive as a side effect.
/.agents/
/.claude/
# Local orchestration loop prompts; machine-local operator state, not repository contract.
/.loops/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# Anchored, plus the two places nested build directories actually occur: an
# unanchored `target/` also swallows source modules named `target`, and a file
# added under `crates/*/src/target/` would silently vanish from `git add`.
# `crates/*/target/` is trybuild's nested cargo invocation, not a source path.
/target/
spikes/*/*/target/
crates/*/target/
/.worktrees/
# Compiler crash reports are regenerable diagnostics, not repository evidence.
/rustc-ice-*.txt
# Locally retained primary-source bytes. Every document under here was read and
# its licence resolved fail-closed: the notices grant copying only where copies
# are not distributed for commercial advantage, and the ACM ones name posting on
# a server explicitly, which is what checking a file in would be. Keeping the
# bytes on one machine is not distribution, so they stay re-readable here while
# the repository carries only our own distilled notes about them and a digest to
# re-acquire against. Anchored to this one directory on purpose: an unanchored
# `*.pdf` would swallow `docs/research/apple-targets/sources/`, whose three
# specifications are deliberately tracked.
/docs/research/cost-model/sources/local/
